(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/emit.asl#" :text "Clean C11 backend emitter consuming verified asl-ir under Address/Undefined Sanitizers")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/emit.asl#emitC11Expr" :text "Emits C11 expression source code for an IR expression.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/emit.asl#emitC11Stmt" :text "Emits C11 source code for a single IR statement.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/emit.asl#emitC11Block" :text "Emits a sequence of C11 statements from an IR statement list.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/emit.asl#emitC11Module" :text "Verifies and emits C11 source code for a complete IR module.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/emit.asl#emitC11StandaloneCase" :text "Emits a self-contained C11 test program for a specific runtime case.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/emit.asl#C11SEnv.functions" :text "Module functions by name")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/emit.asl#C11SEnv.types" :text "ADT name to declared variants in tag order")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/emit.asl#c11SEsc" :text "Encodes an arbitrary ASL identifier as a valid C identifier fragment, escaping any byte outside [A-Za-z0-9_] as _HH.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/emit.asl#c11SType" :text "ptr and i32 (asl-target-llvm/ssa's native C ABI externs, plan RT unit S2) have no asl-target-c lowering yet: the arms below are only for match exhaustiveness.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/emit.asl#c11SStrLit" :text "A C11 string literal for s, using octal escapes (fixed 3 digits, so no following digit is swallowed) for bytes outside printable ASCII.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/emit.asl#c11SArrayLit" :text "A compound literal array of the C type, or a typed null pointer when there are no items.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/emit.asl#c11BuiltinSym" :text "The C symbol a builtin entry calls: asl_rt_b_<symbol> (asl/host/src/abi.c) for a wrap-kind entry, or the libm symbol directly for intrinsic/libm kinds (floor, ceil, round, sqrt, pow, exp, log, log2, log10, sin, cos, tan, atan2 are math.h's own names, so no asl_rt_b_ wrapper and no extra prototype needed).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/emit.asl#c11SOpExpr" :text "The pure C11 expression computing a non-prim SSA op; opPrim is handled statement-wise by c11SPrimStmt before this is reached.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/emit.asl#c11SPrimStmt" :text "Raw primitive arithmetic, comparison and conversion (asl-ir/types primSignature), trapping via __builtin_trap on Int overflow, a zero or INT64_MIN/-1 divisor, or floatToInt out of int64 range, matching asl-target-llvm/ssa's overflowPrim, quotPrim, remPrim and floatToIntPrim.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/emit.asl#c11SRuntimePreamble" :text "extern C prototypes for the host runtime ABI defined in asl/host/src/abi.c, a Val passed by value as AslVal (asl/host/src/value.h Val), the same functions asl-target-llvm/ssa declares for LLVM; the emitted program links against asl/host/out/libaslrt.a.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/emit.asl#c11SEntryProto" :text "A wrap-kind entry's extern prototype; intrinsic/libm kinds (floor, ceil, round, sqrt, pow, exp, log, log2, log10, sin, cos, tan, atan2) call the libm symbol directly (c11BuiltinSym) and need no prototype of our own, math.h already declares them.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/emit.asl#emitC11Source" :text "Compiles ASL source to a standalone C11 program: lowers to the asl-ir SSA contract (asl-ir/lower lowerSource), verifies it (asl-ir/verify verifySsa), and emits C11 calling the same asl_rt_* runtime ABI asl-target-llvm/ssa targets, linkable against asl/host/out/libaslrt.a; the entry is the module's main, taking no arguments or one Val argument list, as asl-host run accepts.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/emit.asl#emitC11SourceWith" :text "emitC11Source over asl-ir/link lowerSourceWith: the prelude functions the module reaches, transitively, are lowered from preludeSrc into the program.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/emit.asl#C11SEnv" :text "emitC11Source (plan SH unit RP3) lowers real ASL source to the asl-ir SSA contract (asl-ir/lower) and emits a standalone C11 program that calls the same asl_rt_* runtime ABI asl-target-llvm/ssa targets, so it links directly against asl/host/out/libaslrt.a; the C11SXxx helpers below are a C-text transliteration of asl-target-llvm/src/ssa.asl's SSA walk, using compound literals in place of alloca+GEP for argument arrays and goto+shared locals in place of phi nodes for block parameters")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/main.asl#" :text "Standalone C11 backend consuming verified asl-ir with Address/Undefined Sanitizers")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/main.asl#emitC11Type" :text "Emits the C11 type name corresponding to an IR type.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/main.asl#emitC11Closure" :text "Emits a C11 environment typedef struct for a closure.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/main.asl#emitC11Panic" :text "Emits C11 code to print a panic error message and exit.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/main.asl#emitC11Block" :text "Emits a sequential block of C11 statements.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/main.asl#emitC11Module" :text "Emits C11 source code for a complete IR module.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/main.asl#emitC11StandaloneCase" :text "Emits C11 standalone code for a specific runtime test case.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/main.asl#emitC11Source" :text "Translates ASL source text into C11 source code.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/main.asl#emitC11SourceWith" :text "Translates ASL source text into C11 source code, linking the prelude functions it reaches from preludeSrc.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/types.asl#" :text "C11 backend type mapping, closure environment synthesis, and panic generation")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/types.asl#emitC11Type" :text "Maps an IR type to its C11 type name representation.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/types.asl#emitC11Closure" :text "Emits a C11 environment struct definition for a closure.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/src/types.asl#emitC11Panic" :text "Emits a C11 statement that prints a panic message to stderr and exits.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/tests/runParityCTest.asl#" :text "Emission-and-syntax gate for the C11 backend (D-targetCRetireNativeLink): the C11 backend is frozen (LLVM is the only executed target), so this no longer links or runs the emitted C against asl/host/out/libaslrt.a. Each corpus program still has to emit via asl-target-c/emit emitC11SourceWith against asl/prelude/prelude.asl, and the emitted C still has to be accepted by /usr/bin/cc -fsyntax-only; link and execution are retired.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/tests/runParityCTest.asl#corpusFiles" :text "The shared run-parity corpus (tests/acceptance/targetParity/corpus)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/tests/runParityCTest.asl#emitAndCheckSyntax" :text "Emits path to C11 and runs /usr/bin/cc -fsyntax-only on it, without linking or running it. The emitted file declares its own extern asl_rt_* prototypes inline (asl-target-c/src/emit.asl emitC11Prologue), so -fsyntax-only needs no header path and no libaslrt.a. err covers read/emit/write failures only; the cc result comes back whole, whatever its exit code, so the caller's assertion on it is the one that fails when cc rejects the C (D152).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/tests/runParityCTest.asl#testCorpusFile" :text "One assertion per corpus file, named by its path: emission succeeds and /usr/bin/cc -fsyntax-only accepts the emitted C with exit code 0. No link, no run, no host-output comparison (frozen backend, D-targetCRetireNativeLink).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/tests/runParityCTest.asl#testMathBuiltinsC" :text "P5 r2: sqrt/floor/ceil/round, no longer backed by asl_rt_b_<symbol> in abi.c (deleted), and pow/exp/log/log2/log10/sin/cos/tan/atan2 (newly lowered from source) still have to emit and syntax-check through the C target, not just LLVM: not in the shared corpusFiles list (that list's count is asserted by runParity's own ts/llvm parity tests), so testing it here is additive.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/tests/targetCTest.asl#" :text "Unit tests for asl-target-c C11 backend emitter and types")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/tests/targetCTest.asl#testC11SourceCompiles" :text "emitC11Source (plan SH unit RP3) lowers a real program through asl-ir/lower and emits a C11 program calling the host runtime ABI, no longer a canned refusal.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/tests/targetCTest.asl#testC11SourceNullaryConstruct" :text "A nullary enum variant (0 fields) exercises c11SArrayLit's empty-argument branch, a typed null pointer rather than a zero-length compound literal.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-target-c/tests/targetCTest.asl#testC11MainWrapperRecordReturn" :text "c11SMainWrapper's tyRec arm (RT mutant M10): the lowerer always gives the program entry a Val signature (asl-ir/lower sigOf), so a record-returning entry is unreachable through emitC11Source; this calls the emitter helper directly with a synthetic SsaFunction to cover the arm anyway.")
